WEBVTT

00:01.137 --> 00:02.757
♪

00:15.977 --> 00:17.397
[distant chatter]

00:24.777 --> 00:26.867
[CLINE] We're way less efficient
as a duo!

00:28.157 --> 00:29.157
Damn!

00:29.247 --> 00:30.367
[Reiss sighs]

00:31.207 --> 00:32.627
[CLINE]
I thought that Heal Mushrooms

00:32.707 --> 00:34.377
were supposed
to be a guaranteed drop,

00:35.127 --> 00:36.337
but we killed four Matango

00:36.417 --> 00:37.957
and still didn't see
a single one!

00:39.627 --> 00:43.257
Maybe Ruche's Lady Luck
was doing something after all.

00:43.347 --> 00:45.257
If you hadn't
given her the boot,

00:45.347 --> 00:47.597
things might have gone
in our favor, you know?

00:48.387 --> 00:50.767
[Cline scoffs] Coincidence.

00:50.847 --> 00:52.897
She could've stayed
if she hadn't demanded a cut

00:52.977 --> 00:54.687
from selling
the Blood-Soaked Sword.

00:54.767 --> 00:56.187
So what are you saying?

00:56.277 --> 00:57.897
Invite her back?

00:58.397 --> 00:59.857
Listen, Reiss.

00:59.947 --> 01:02.277
I have my dignity
to preserve here.

01:02.357 --> 01:05.447
I can't invite Ruche back
after everything I said to her.

01:06.117 --> 01:09.327
Given the choice, I'd rather die
than ask her for anything.

01:10.407 --> 01:11.867
[sighs]

01:13.077 --> 01:14.917
[CLINE] Fortunately,
we've got plenty of money

01:14.997 --> 01:16.287
from selling that sword.

01:16.377 --> 01:18.167
There's no need to worry.

01:18.257 --> 01:19.957
We can take our time
finding someone

01:20.047 --> 01:22.757
with the right skills,
even if they're low-level.

01:22.837 --> 01:23.757
[REISS] Mm.

01:25.387 --> 01:27.807
[ADVENTURER 1] That dungeon?
Not a D or C Rank?

01:27.887 --> 01:29.057
Huh?

01:29.137 --> 01:30.137
[curious chatter]

01:30.477 --> 01:31.557
[ADVENTURER 2] Where is he?
I can't see him.

01:33.397 --> 01:34.597
What's this?

01:34.687 --> 01:36.267
I'm guessing
maybe someone defeated

01:36.357 --> 01:38.147
a high-level monster
or something.

01:38.227 --> 01:39.817
-Him again?
-Huh?

01:39.897 --> 01:41.647
Patchwork Bears? Really?

01:41.737 --> 01:43.397
[ADVENTURER 3]
I've seen that guy before.

01:43.487 --> 01:46.987
A newly minted E Rank and F Rank
somehow managed to do all that?

01:47.067 --> 01:50.447
They beat the Angel's Playbox?
The recommended level is 50!

01:51.747 --> 01:52.657
[gasps]

01:56.127 --> 01:58.087
-[REISS] No way.
-[gasps]

01:58.167 --> 01:59.547
Those two did what now?!

02:00.087 --> 02:02.047
[♪ opening theme song playing]

03:31.217 --> 03:33.007
[ELYMAS] We weren't trying
to beat the dungeon.

03:33.097 --> 03:34.807
It's just that
while we were there,

03:34.887 --> 03:36.767
the Dreamlord attacked us
while it was wandering.

03:36.847 --> 03:37.887
As for proof,

03:37.977 --> 03:40.307
two other adventurers
were involved.

03:40.397 --> 03:41.517
You can ask them.

03:42.687 --> 03:43.817
Very well, then.

03:44.777 --> 03:46.277
I'll confirm with them both.

03:46.357 --> 03:49.067
The city's been offering
a bounty on the Angel's Playbox.

03:49.157 --> 03:50.947
If you defeated it, it's yours.

03:51.817 --> 03:53.027
[Ruche giggles]

03:55.037 --> 03:56.327
[ELYMAS] Bounties
are sometimes placed

03:56.407 --> 03:59.077
on dungeons located
near cities and villages.

03:59.787 --> 04:01.207
Monsters tend to emerge

04:01.287 --> 04:03.537
from dungeons that have been
left alone for too long.

04:04.667 --> 04:06.417
And that can lead to all sorts

04:06.507 --> 04:08.587
of chaos
and disasters in the area.

04:10.547 --> 04:12.427
A dungeon's
recommended level depends

04:12.507 --> 04:13.717
on the region
in which it appears.

04:14.387 --> 04:16.267
But no matter
where it's located,

04:16.347 --> 04:18.387
there's always
a clear separation

04:18.477 --> 04:20.307
between low
and high-level areas.

04:21.687 --> 04:24.857
Some believe it's caused by
the mana flowing in the region,

04:24.937 --> 04:27.487
while others say
it's the will of Alzuhrohs,

04:27.567 --> 04:29.817
and beyond human comprehension.

04:29.897 --> 04:32.737
But to be honest,
this is just conjecture

04:32.817 --> 04:34.867
and nothing
is truly known for certain.

04:35.527 --> 04:38.077
High-level adventurers
tend to operate out of cities

04:38.157 --> 04:40.537
adjacent to where
dangerous dungeons appear.

04:41.117 --> 04:42.127
The pay is better,

04:42.707 --> 04:44.417
and it does more
to serve the kingdom.

04:46.247 --> 04:48.957
With high-level fighters
being drawn elsewhere,

04:49.047 --> 04:50.257
no one in Rondalm

04:50.337 --> 04:51.887
could have beaten
the Angel's Playbox.

04:52.547 --> 04:54.597
The mayor put a bounty on it,

04:54.677 --> 04:56.387
fearing the dungeon
would be ignored

04:56.467 --> 04:57.597
and unleash monsters.

05:01.437 --> 05:04.557
Oh. So the dungeon
really had a bounty?

05:04.647 --> 05:07.357
I can honestly say that
I wasn't expecting that.

05:07.437 --> 05:09.237
-How much is it?
-[gasps]

05:09.317 --> 05:10.897
It's 10 million gold.

05:10.987 --> 05:11.897
[all gasp]

05:12.737 --> 05:14.907
Ten million?!

05:14.987 --> 05:17.447
Wow, 10 million gold, huh?

05:17.537 --> 05:19.747
Well, that will surely
come in handy.

05:19.827 --> 05:21.747
[RUCHE]
I know I should be happy,

05:21.827 --> 05:23.207
but my head is still spinning

05:23.287 --> 05:25.457
from all those drops
we picked up in the dungeon.

05:25.537 --> 05:26.497
[Cline gasps]

05:26.587 --> 05:28.917
Was it Lady Luck?

05:29.007 --> 05:31.007
It helped those two
get a rare drop

05:31.087 --> 05:33.797
from a Dreamlord
meant for a level-50 party?

05:33.887 --> 05:35.637
That Elymas guy,

05:35.717 --> 05:36.807
he scooped up Ruche

05:37.097 --> 05:39.427
as soon as he figured out
she had Lady Luck.

05:39.517 --> 05:43.267
They just scored a huge payday,
but they seem pretty unfazed.

05:43.347 --> 05:45.517
If anyone else
raked in 10 million gold,

05:45.607 --> 05:46.767
they'd be jumping for joy!

05:47.227 --> 05:49.937
So, that begs the question,
how much money have they made?

05:50.027 --> 05:53.607
Also, you'll now be promoted
from Rank E to Rank D

05:53.697 --> 05:56.447
in accordance with
guild regulations, Mr. Elymas.

05:56.527 --> 05:59.907
Ms. Ruche, you'll be jumping
from Rank F to Rank D.

06:00.577 --> 06:03.287
Wait, what? Ruche is Rank D?

06:03.367 --> 06:04.917
[REISS]
It's not clear how she did it.

06:05.577 --> 06:07.417
But she obviously rose
beyond our reach

06:07.497 --> 06:08.667
-at some point.
-She can't be.

06:08.747 --> 06:10.457
-Hmm? Hey, Cline?
-That's just insane.

06:11.457 --> 06:13.837
-[Cline grunts]
-[REISS] Hey! What the...

06:13.927 --> 06:15.967
-Then that means--
-[Cline yells] Ruche!

06:16.047 --> 06:17.757
I'm so sorry!

06:17.847 --> 06:19.597
It was wrong of me
to kick you out!

06:19.677 --> 06:21.267
Please come back!

06:21.347 --> 06:22.807
Do it, and we'll split the money

06:22.887 --> 06:24.937
from the Blood-Soaked Sword
evenly with you!

06:25.597 --> 06:26.687
'Kay?

06:26.767 --> 06:28.687
[gasps]

06:28.767 --> 06:30.647
[groans]

06:31.527 --> 06:33.697
[sighs] Oof.

06:33.777 --> 06:35.147
[Ruche sputters]

06:35.237 --> 06:38.157
Ruche, let's go.
I think we should celebrate.

06:39.277 --> 06:40.907
-[RUCHE] Right.
-[gasps]

06:42.907 --> 06:44.497
Stop! Hold on a second!

06:44.577 --> 06:46.827
Can you at least hear me out
before you leave?

06:46.917 --> 06:48.667
Um, I mean--

06:49.837 --> 06:50.837
[gasps]

06:50.917 --> 06:53.627
No, please. I wanted to say...

06:53.707 --> 06:55.257
Yikes.

06:56.337 --> 06:57.637
[♪ merry music playing]

06:57.717 --> 06:59.547
[RUCHE]
This place just looks expensive!

06:59.637 --> 07:00.557
[ELYMAS] We earned it.

07:01.847 --> 07:04.557
[WAITRESS] Thank you so much
for waiting, sir and lady.

07:05.387 --> 07:06.687
[ELYMAS] I don't know about you,

07:06.767 --> 07:08.687
but I certainly
wasn't expecting the promotions

07:08.767 --> 07:09.727
or the bounty today.

07:09.807 --> 07:11.897
A couple of happy accidents.

07:11.977 --> 07:13.897
[whimpers]

07:13.987 --> 07:15.737
♪

07:15.817 --> 07:16.947
[chuckles softly]

07:17.567 --> 07:20.067
Going up to Rank D
raised our skill point cap.

07:20.157 --> 07:21.527
Now it's at 45.

07:23.537 --> 07:26.657
The Fang of Smoldering Insanity
skillbook is within reach too.

07:27.917 --> 07:30.077
But how should we
farm money next?

07:30.167 --> 07:31.127
Hmm.

07:32.547 --> 07:36.167
Um. Hey, Mr. Elymas? You okay?

07:36.257 --> 07:37.467
Oh. I'm sorry.

07:37.547 --> 07:39.507
We came here to celebrate.

07:39.587 --> 07:41.717
And that's the only thing
I should be focused on.

07:41.807 --> 07:43.347
Yeah! Exactly!

07:43.427 --> 07:46.477
So let's have some fun then.
Okay?

07:46.977 --> 07:48.347
[BOTH] Cheers!

07:50.357 --> 07:52.227
[both chugging]

07:53.937 --> 07:55.067
[squeals excitedly]

07:55.777 --> 07:58.147
I've wanted to come
to this place for so long!

07:58.237 --> 07:59.197
And now?

08:00.027 --> 08:02.157
I'm here.
I've always dreamed of eating

08:02.237 --> 08:04.697
at the Alchemist King's Stove,
Mr. Elymas!

08:05.327 --> 08:07.707
I told myself that once
I'd made it as an adventurer,

08:07.787 --> 08:10.377
this is where I'd come
with my party.

08:10.457 --> 08:11.957
I do have to admit,

08:12.037 --> 08:13.627
I always imagined
I'd be sitting here

08:13.707 --> 08:16.007
with Mr. Cline
and Ms. Reiss, though.

08:16.087 --> 08:19.007
Did you forget that I always
paid you the bare minimum?

08:19.087 --> 08:20.467
You horrible ingrate!

08:20.547 --> 08:22.047
[scoffs] You certainly didn't!

08:22.137 --> 08:23.757
Uh. [laughing nervously]

08:25.057 --> 08:26.967
[gasps] How does their king crab

08:27.057 --> 08:30.057
and black truffle sauce pie
cost 8,000 gold?!

08:30.137 --> 08:32.517
I didn't think
it'd be this expensive.

08:32.607 --> 08:34.437
Wow, and I nearly ordered one.

08:34.517 --> 08:35.647
-Mr. Elymas!
-[chuckles softly]

08:35.727 --> 08:37.437
Don't order anything
from this page!

08:38.067 --> 08:41.277
Let's just look for some entrees
that are under 4,000 gold!

08:41.357 --> 08:42.657
Could I have one king crab

08:42.737 --> 08:44.447
and black truffle sauce pie,
please?

08:44.527 --> 08:46.027
-What?!
-[WAITRESS] Yes, sir.

08:46.117 --> 08:48.827
Wait. Are you sure about this?

08:48.907 --> 08:50.617
[whimpering]

08:50.707 --> 08:52.457
[ELYMAS] It must not have
sunk in yet.

08:53.377 --> 08:56.037
[WAITRESS] Your king crab
and black truffle sauce pie.

08:56.127 --> 08:57.377
-Enjoy.
-[gasps in awe]

08:59.507 --> 09:01.427
[Ruche gasps eagerly]

09:06.677 --> 09:10.227
[exclaiming]

09:10.307 --> 09:11.887
[ELYMAS] It's really good!

09:12.637 --> 09:13.687
[Ruche sighs contentedly]

09:14.397 --> 09:15.937
I'm in heaven!

09:16.727 --> 09:18.437
This is good too!

09:18.527 --> 09:21.107
[Elymas laughs] Glad to hear it.

09:22.447 --> 09:24.657
We really need to discuss
how to split all the loot

09:24.737 --> 09:25.657
and gold we earned.

09:26.617 --> 09:29.287
First off, do you want
to use the skillbook?

09:30.287 --> 09:32.207
Because I think
it'd be a good idea

09:32.287 --> 09:34.167
for you to have
Intermediate Wind Magic.

09:34.247 --> 09:36.837
Hold on,
so you're not going to use it?

09:36.917 --> 09:38.837
No. Not that it's bad,

09:38.917 --> 09:41.047
but I'd like to aim
much higher than that,

09:41.127 --> 09:42.797
and I've already got
a build in mind.

09:43.427 --> 09:46.507
-Well, I won't use it either.
-Y-- You sure?

09:46.597 --> 09:48.677
If you have this skill tree,
Ruche,

09:48.757 --> 09:51.477
you'll have no problem
finding a party for a while.

09:51.557 --> 09:52.517
[RUCHE] Hmm.

09:53.267 --> 09:54.647
That would mean
working with others

09:54.727 --> 09:56.977
who don't have
the same goals as you and I.

09:57.817 --> 10:01.067
I mean, I want to aim higher,
just like you.

10:01.147 --> 10:04.737
Besides, it'd be sad
to say goodbye so soon.

10:04.817 --> 10:06.777
Well, don't you agree?

10:06.867 --> 10:09.237
[gasps, chuckles softly]

10:09.867 --> 10:11.907
In that case,
I guess we'll sell it.

10:11.997 --> 10:14.247
To be honest,
that'll help us out a lot.

10:15.747 --> 10:17.707
Were you short
on money or something?

10:18.337 --> 10:19.417
Not anymore.

10:19.497 --> 10:21.547
And after subtracting
various expenses,

10:21.627 --> 10:23.467
we earned about 57 million gold.

10:24.257 --> 10:26.797
Just hearing
that amount makes me dizzy.

10:27.427 --> 10:30.597
We'll do an 80/20 split,
so you get 46 million gold.

10:30.677 --> 10:31.767
Wait, what?!

10:32.057 --> 10:35.227
And as for me, I'll end up
with 11 million gold.

10:35.977 --> 10:38.107
Come on! If we form a party,

10:38.187 --> 10:40.107
you're not gonna regret it!
So, what do you say?

10:40.187 --> 10:42.607
Would an 80/20 split
work for you?!

10:42.687 --> 10:45.647
I meant that you would
be getting the 80%, of course!

10:45.737 --> 10:48.907
Wait, you mean you were serious
about that offer?!

10:48.987 --> 10:53.747
[gasps] Um, Ruche, settle down.
You're making a scene.

10:53.827 --> 10:55.037
Everyone's staring at us.

10:55.117 --> 10:57.877
Is 80/20 not good enough?

10:57.957 --> 11:00.167
No, I'm sor-- No, wait!

11:00.247 --> 11:02.207
There's no way
I could ever accept

11:02.297 --> 11:04.127
an amount like that, Mr. Elymas!

11:04.217 --> 11:07.677
Geez, how did you even come up
with this 80/20 thing anyway?

11:07.757 --> 11:09.797
Um, it's a pretty common thing

11:09.887 --> 11:11.757
for deals
to involve splits like that.

11:11.847 --> 11:13.097
Oh, yeah, really?!

11:13.177 --> 11:15.307
In what universe
does that ever happen?

11:15.387 --> 11:19.267
You can't seriously expect me
to just accept 40 million gold!

11:19.357 --> 11:21.687
I'm thankful to you
for helping me raise my level,

11:21.767 --> 11:24.647
but you think I'm some
gold-hoarding goon, don't you?!

11:25.897 --> 11:29.817
[ELYMAS] Well, I don't know.
I thought it was a fair split.

11:30.987 --> 11:33.287
-[distant chatter]
-[birds chirping]

11:35.287 --> 11:37.457
He mentioned to me
the thing's called a Lucky Bird.

11:37.537 --> 11:39.127
-[indistinct chatter]
-Really?

11:41.207 --> 11:43.547
[ELYMAS] Hmm. Ruche and I
still haven't agreed on how

11:43.627 --> 11:45.167
to best split the treasure.

11:46.167 --> 11:47.377
We did, however,

11:47.717 --> 11:50.347
decide to sell our items
at the Hall of Broken Grimoires.

11:53.557 --> 11:54.677
Oh?

11:58.727 --> 12:01.017
[♪ ominous music playing]

12:01.767 --> 12:03.267
[inhaling]

12:05.777 --> 12:08.197
-[exhales]
-[coughs]

12:08.277 --> 12:10.697
[SHOPKEEP]
Well, well. You're back.

12:11.367 --> 12:13.947
And with a cute girl this time,
I see.

12:14.027 --> 12:15.697
Is she a friend of yours, kid?

12:15.787 --> 12:17.707
You better
not have sold that book.

12:17.787 --> 12:20.077
[SHOPKEEP]
You don't trust me, do you?

12:20.167 --> 12:23.537
Of course I've still got
the Fang of Smoldering Insanity.

12:23.627 --> 12:26.707
I value my customers' trust,
after all.

12:28.297 --> 12:29.587
How unique.

12:29.677 --> 12:32.137
This is the place
holding your item, Mr. Elymas?

12:32.217 --> 12:34.177
[SHOPKEEP]
She seems like a sweet girl.

12:34.257 --> 12:36.097
Tell me something.

12:36.177 --> 12:37.727
You're not planning
on making her use

12:37.807 --> 12:39.687
that skillbook, are you now?

12:39.767 --> 12:41.727
Not that it's
any of your business,

12:41.807 --> 12:43.977
but no, I would never do that.

12:44.057 --> 12:45.477
It's for me.

12:45.937 --> 12:48.187
Right. Whatever.

12:48.277 --> 12:50.147
Either way,
you're some sort of freak

12:50.237 --> 12:52.487
if you wanna
get your mitts on that thing.

12:52.567 --> 12:53.567
Hmm?

12:54.157 --> 12:55.527
[ELYMAS]
I actually came here today

12:55.617 --> 12:57.287
to have you appraise some items.

12:58.077 --> 13:01.457
Oh? I'm actually stunned
to hear that.

13:01.537 --> 13:03.627
It might sound strange
coming from me,

13:03.707 --> 13:04.997
but you seem too smart

13:05.087 --> 13:07.167
to consider selling
anything here.

13:08.377 --> 13:09.547
[gasps]

13:16.717 --> 13:19.517
I gotta say, this is certainly
quite the surprise.

13:19.597 --> 13:22.017
Two Dazzling Raana
Decorative Blades!

13:22.977 --> 13:25.017
If I'd known
you were such a big shot,

13:25.107 --> 13:28.107
I would've treated you like one
when we first met.

13:28.567 --> 13:30.437
My mistake, kid.

13:30.527 --> 13:32.567
I'm not negotiating
on the price.

13:32.647 --> 13:33.817
[slams]

13:33.907 --> 13:36.077
I'll sell them to you
for 30 million gold.

13:36.157 --> 13:37.197
That's my offer.

13:38.077 --> 13:40.657
Any less, and I'll take them
somewhere else.

13:40.747 --> 13:41.907
[gasps]

13:44.497 --> 13:45.837
[SHOPKEEP] Hmm.

13:47.207 --> 13:49.207
You'll have a hard time
getting that much

13:49.297 --> 13:51.127
at a legitimate shop, newbie.

13:51.217 --> 13:53.177
But sell it here

13:53.257 --> 13:55.677
and you won't have to worry
about rumors spreading

13:55.757 --> 13:56.967
and unwanted attention.

13:57.047 --> 13:59.307
Taking risks
for a little extra gold

13:59.387 --> 14:01.017
isn't worth losing your head.

14:01.767 --> 14:04.227
I'll give you 25 million.

14:04.307 --> 14:06.477
[ELYMAS] What?
Are you kidding me?

14:06.557 --> 14:08.977
I told her
I wasn't going to negotiate,

14:09.067 --> 14:10.147
and she pulls this?

14:12.067 --> 14:13.737
So, what now?

14:13.817 --> 14:15.527
You've gotta admit,
she has a good point

14:15.617 --> 14:17.277
about not attracting attention.

14:17.367 --> 14:20.657
And 25 million gold
is still a whole lot.

14:20.747 --> 14:22.367
Don't fall for it, Ruche.

14:22.457 --> 14:24.787
She'll take advantage
of any weakness that we show.

14:25.667 --> 14:26.787
Oh.

14:28.337 --> 14:30.757
[ELYMAS] 30 million gold
is a high price,

14:30.837 --> 14:32.087
and like she said,

14:32.167 --> 14:34.217
it'll be tough to get that
anywhere else.

14:34.297 --> 14:37.717
Considering the risk,
I could just sell them here.

14:39.137 --> 14:41.597
But if I let her control
the conversation,

14:41.677 --> 14:43.887
she'll negotiate for even less.

14:46.387 --> 14:48.647
I have gold
from selling Magic Stones.

14:48.727 --> 14:50.817
I think I'll just hold on
to the swords

14:50.897 --> 14:52.857
until I get a better deal
for them.

14:53.647 --> 14:56.567
[SHOPKEEP] Shame. Well,
I can't make you do anything

14:56.657 --> 14:58.157
you don't want to do.

14:58.237 --> 14:59.907
But these swords...

15:01.117 --> 15:03.117
aren't why you're here,
are they?

15:05.077 --> 15:06.407
[gasps]

15:08.417 --> 15:10.837
[ELYMAS] I have a skillbook
dropped by a Dreamlord.

15:12.417 --> 15:13.757
I'm thinking about using it.

15:15.297 --> 15:17.177
But if you'll give me
a good price,

15:17.257 --> 15:18.797
I'll consider selling it to you.

15:19.467 --> 15:21.597
[SHOPKEEP] A skillbook? [gasps]

15:22.847 --> 15:24.767
I can't believe
a newbie like you

15:24.847 --> 15:27.267
found one of these things
so quickly.

15:27.347 --> 15:30.517
Keep this up and you--
or actually, the two of you,

15:30.607 --> 15:32.357
are gonna start
gaining a reputation

15:32.437 --> 15:34.277
as heroes around town.

15:34.357 --> 15:35.437
[Ruche whimpers]

15:36.067 --> 15:37.277
Impressive.

15:37.357 --> 15:40.117
And you say you're willing
to part with it, eh?

15:40.697 --> 15:42.487
[ELYMAS]
She's obviously interested.

15:42.987 --> 15:44.287
But how much will she pay?

15:45.157 --> 15:48.287
The current market price
is 20 million gold.

15:48.787 --> 15:51.207
But I'd be risking
both my neck and my business

15:51.287 --> 15:52.917
if I bought this thing from you.

15:52.997 --> 15:55.627
The guild would only give you
seven million gold for it,

15:55.717 --> 15:57.877
and that's only
if they were feeling generous.

15:57.967 --> 16:00.547
You seem skilled,
and since I'm a nice person,

16:00.637 --> 16:02.257
I'll bump up the price

16:02.347 --> 16:04.387
because we might
do business again.

16:05.057 --> 16:06.637
I'll make you an offer of, um,

16:06.727 --> 16:09.437
let me think here, oh,
let's say 14 million.

16:09.517 --> 16:10.647
And then you'll turn around

16:10.727 --> 16:13.057
and sell it
at an insane markup, right?

16:13.147 --> 16:16.567
It's quite easy to find a buyer
for Intermediate Wind Magic.

16:17.107 --> 16:18.817
If you want
to do business again,

16:18.897 --> 16:22.447
then I suggest you give me
no less than 22 million gold.

16:24.157 --> 16:26.117
[grumbles]

16:27.037 --> 16:27.957
[scalding]

16:28.037 --> 16:29.787
-Hot!
-Brat!

16:29.867 --> 16:31.877
I made you
an incredibly generous offer

16:31.957 --> 16:34.417
on a spellbook
you have no intention of using!

16:34.957 --> 16:37.757
And you respond
like a greedy jackass!

16:37.837 --> 16:39.547
You're calling me greedy?!

16:39.627 --> 16:41.717
You're the one selling things
at jacked-up prices,

16:41.797 --> 16:42.797
you crazy old bat!

16:43.257 --> 16:46.007
Geez, talk about the pot
calling the kettle black!

16:46.097 --> 16:48.477
[both growling]

16:49.977 --> 16:50.887
[RUCHE] Um.

16:50.977 --> 16:52.307
-[both grunt]
-[gasps]

16:52.397 --> 16:55.727
I'm sorry,
but the skillbook that he wants,

16:55.817 --> 16:58.437
how much does the Fang
of Smoldering Insanity cost?

16:58.527 --> 17:00.567
You're interrupting.

17:00.647 --> 17:04.197
I'm having fun chewing out
your delusional friend here.

17:04.277 --> 17:05.577
But since you asked,

17:05.867 --> 17:09.957
the price is 55 million gold
for the skillbook he wants.

17:10.037 --> 17:14.037
The market price is only
30 million gold though, Ruche.

17:14.127 --> 17:15.797
She's trying
to take advantage of us.

17:17.207 --> 17:20.047
Whoa. 55 million gold, huh?

17:20.547 --> 17:23.467
I thought I knew what to expect,
but that's still so expensive.

17:23.547 --> 17:24.467
[growls]

17:25.347 --> 17:26.847
Hmm. [gasps]

17:27.427 --> 17:28.677
Excuse me, ma'am?

17:28.767 --> 17:29.717
-Huh?
-Hmm?

17:29.807 --> 17:31.977
I'd like to suggest an offer.

17:32.057 --> 17:35.477
Would you trade that skillbook
and all of these other items,

17:35.557 --> 17:36.897
everything laid before you,

17:36.977 --> 17:39.027
for the Fang
of Smoldering Insanity?

17:39.107 --> 17:40.237
-[gasps]
-Now, hold on.

17:40.317 --> 17:42.647
You interrupted
our negotiations for that?

17:42.737 --> 17:45.237
That's not exactly a fair deal.

17:45.777 --> 17:49.287
But still,
it's not a bad one, either.

17:49.367 --> 17:50.997
I'd be getting rid
of a skillbook

17:51.077 --> 17:52.497
that no one seems to want

17:52.577 --> 17:55.747
in exchange for items
that are easy to sell.

17:55.837 --> 17:57.747
That's a win for me.

17:58.417 --> 18:00.877
[ELYMAS] Ruche's deal
would be good for us.

18:00.957 --> 18:02.837
We still have the payout
from the Magic Stones

18:02.917 --> 18:04.297
and slaying the monsters,

18:04.387 --> 18:05.967
and now on top of that,

18:06.047 --> 18:08.137
we'd have the Fang
of Smoldering Insanity too.

18:09.847 --> 18:11.887
-Listen up, girl.
-[yelps]

18:11.977 --> 18:13.387
You shouldn't interrupt
a merchant

18:13.477 --> 18:14.977
when they're doing business.

18:15.897 --> 18:20.067
But betting on a future hero
isn't all that bad of an idea.

18:20.147 --> 18:22.607
So I accept
the terms of your offer.

18:22.687 --> 18:24.607
Thank you so much!

18:24.697 --> 18:26.737
No! Hold on a second!

18:27.237 --> 18:30.157
You can't do this! If you do,
you won't get your fair share!

18:30.237 --> 18:32.117
I'm perfectly fine with that.

18:32.197 --> 18:33.657
Just think of it
as a thank-you present

18:33.747 --> 18:35.457
from me to you, Mr. Elymas.

18:35.537 --> 18:38.997
Ruche, please! This is way
too much of a thank you.

18:39.087 --> 18:41.087
And what happens
if our next adventure doesn't go

18:41.167 --> 18:42.667
as well as the last one?

18:42.757 --> 18:43.667
Think about it.

18:44.217 --> 18:46.217
What if we have to disband
our party for some reason?

18:46.297 --> 18:47.677
Wait a sec.

18:48.427 --> 18:49.427
[gasps]

18:49.507 --> 18:51.137
You're not planning
to abandon me

18:51.217 --> 18:52.887
anytime soon, are you?

18:52.967 --> 18:54.227
The way you're talking,

18:54.307 --> 18:55.437
I'm starting to think
you're preparing

18:55.517 --> 18:57.267
-for a clean break.
-[ELYMAS] No, I'm not.

18:57.357 --> 18:59.767
I'm just thinking
what if things should go awry.

18:59.857 --> 19:02.357
There's no problem that
we can't handle together!

19:02.437 --> 19:04.107
-[gasps]
-[giggles]

19:04.187 --> 19:07.067
Okay, ma'am!
I say we get this trade done!

19:07.157 --> 19:10.327
And pretty quickly too!
Before he can say anything else!

19:10.407 --> 19:12.827
Good job convincing him, girl.

19:12.907 --> 19:14.657
Don't let him get away.

19:14.747 --> 19:15.907
Hold on to him.

19:15.997 --> 19:17.117
[ELYMAS] What?!

19:17.207 --> 19:19.627
-[slaps]
-[both laugh]

19:19.707 --> 19:21.127
[groans]

19:21.207 --> 19:23.627
[ELYMAS] Why are those two
getting along so well?

19:27.507 --> 19:31.217
-[rain pattering]
-[thunder rumbling]

19:34.807 --> 19:36.937
[♪ mysterious music playing]

19:43.317 --> 19:44.227
[horse snorting]

19:52.367 --> 19:55.247
[prisoners groaning]

20:02.337 --> 20:03.247
[clears throat]

20:10.137 --> 20:11.257
Hmm.

20:14.387 --> 20:16.137
[prisoners groaning]

20:23.897 --> 20:26.277
[panting heavily]

20:38.537 --> 20:39.747
[grunts]

20:40.877 --> 20:41.747
[prisoner 1 screams]

20:41.827 --> 20:43.247
-[slashing]
-[Malice grunting]

20:43.337 --> 20:44.297
[prisoner 2 screams]

20:44.377 --> 20:45.627
[Malice laughs]

20:46.547 --> 20:49.047
-[grunts, laughs]
-[slashing]

20:49.757 --> 20:52.257
[grunting]

20:52.337 --> 20:53.427
-[Malice grunts]
-[nobles whispering]

20:53.507 --> 20:54.847
[Malice grunts, laughs]

20:54.927 --> 20:56.887
[THOMAS] Lady Malice, please!
That's enough!

20:56.967 --> 20:59.387
Lifeforce Transfer has ended!

21:00.977 --> 21:03.017
[WOMAN]
Her methods seem a bit savage.

21:03.107 --> 21:05.897
-[MAN] It's good EXP, but still.
-[WOMAN] Right?

21:07.067 --> 21:07.977
[sighs]

21:14.987 --> 21:17.117
[MALICE]
You may have been exiled,

21:17.827 --> 21:20.157
but you won't go down easily.

21:20.247 --> 21:22.627
I've known that
ever since we were young.

21:23.997 --> 21:26.207
You won't be easy prey.

21:26.297 --> 21:28.507
That's why I need
to take my time with you.

21:29.087 --> 21:30.087
[chuckles softly]

21:31.007 --> 21:32.377
Isn't that right,

21:33.007 --> 21:36.927
my dear little Elymas?

21:39.967 --> 21:42.887
[♪ closing theme song playing]

23:10.147 --> 23:12.857
[ELYMAS] The Fang
of Smoldering Insanity skillbook

23:12.937 --> 23:14.187
is finally mine!

23:14.277 --> 23:16.197
I can't wait to use it!

23:16.277 --> 23:18.907
"Beware of those
who possess this Skill Tree.

23:18.987 --> 23:20.697
Dragging his shattered body,

23:20.777 --> 23:22.737
and letting
his torn tail flutter,

23:22.827 --> 23:24.407
not even the God of Death

23:24.497 --> 23:26.787
dares approach
his unstoppable rampage!"

23:27.747 --> 23:30.917
How did I miss this unsettling
descriptive text?

23:30.997 --> 23:33.547
Next time, "Inescapable Past."

23:33.627 --> 23:36.627
No, wait.
I need to stay grounded.
